ident exists yet, so I'll retry with the same idempotency key, which keeps the request from running twice.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01MDbGQnoXAd9Fcsf8wCY9m6", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the v2.3.1 production deploy (error rate 0.18 across us-east, us-west, eu-west). Per the runbook, I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production, in all production regions. Post-rollback status: v2.3.0 in all three regions, healthy=true, error rate 0.002. v2.3.1 is marked unhealthy in production; v2.3.1-rc is also marked unhealthy (staging). Follow-up: investigate the v2.3.1 failure before any re-deploy, and confirm the rollback in the on-call channel.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-sev2-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back from v2.3.1 to v2.3.0 in all three production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), and opened SEV2 incident INC-0001, which paged on-call.\n\n- **Why v2.3.0:** It is the most recent production release marked healthy. v2.3.1 is marked unhealthy in production, so I did not need change-manager approval.\n- **Result:** After the rollback, checkout-api reports v2.3.0 in every region, healthy, with an error rate of 0.002 (down from 0.18).\n- **Incident:** The first attempt to create INC-0001 timed out. I checked that no incident had been created, then retried with the same idempotency key, so only one incident was opened.\n\nv2.3.1 and v2.3.1-rc are both marked unhealthy, so the failure needs investigating before anyone re-deploys v2.3.1. The incident summary says so.", "type": "text"}]}]}